# ==============================================================================
# Trivy Ignore File - DPN Reference Infrastructure
# ==============================================================================
# AVD IDs are from the Aqua Security Vulnerability Database:
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/azure/
#
# Format: one AVD ID or check ID per line; comments start with #
#
# Trivy's resource-attribute checks generally can't flag "this resource type
# is entirely missing" (e.g. no azurerm_security_center_subscription_pricing
# resource for Defender for Cloud enrollment) - only misconfigured attributes
# on resources that exist. For the fuller picture of accepted-risk items,
# including ones Trivy's rule set doesn't independently catch, see
# .checkov.yaml, which documents each with its rationale.
#
# KNOWN SCAN LIMITATION - verify with isolated module scans, not just the
# full-repo scan: `trivy fs dpn-azure-infrastructure --scanners misconfig
# --tf-vars dpn-azure-infrastructure/environments/dpn_infrastructure.tfvars`
# silently returns zero findings AND zero passes for AVD-AZU-0058 and
# AVD-AZU-0061 specifically - neither check appears in the output at all,
# passing or failing, when the full module graph (root + all 12 child
# modules, with their cross-module output references such as
# module.networking.subnet_ids[...] and conditional CMK key IDs) is
# evaluated together. Confirmed via `trivy fs modules/storage --scanners
# misconfig --include-non-failures` (the storage module scanned on its own,
# with only its own variable defaults) that both checks evaluate correctly
# in isolation - this is a Trivy resolution limitation with this codebase's
# inter-module dependency depth, not a real absence of findings. Re-verify
# with the isolated-module command above after any change to the storage
# module, rather than trusting a clean full-repo `trivy fs` run alone.
# ==============================================================================

# ── Storage account geo-redundancy ────────────────────────────────────────────
# dev_storage / file_scanning_storage / observability_logging_storage use
# locally-redundant storage (LRS) to reduce cost in dev/test tier. Must be
# upgraded to GRS/RAGRS before pre-prod / production, where regional-outage
# durability matters. Confirmed still LRS in dpn_infrastructure.tfvars and
# confirmed the check still correctly FAILs against it via the isolated
# module scan (see limitation note above).
AVD-AZU-0058

# AVD-AZU-0061 (storage infrastructure encryption) is no longer listed here:
# modules/storage now defaults infrastructure_encryption_enabled to true (no
# additional Azure cost, safe for any new deployment since it's only
# ForceNew on an *existing* account). Confirmed PASS via the isolated module
# scan (see limitation note above).
